WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.990
Move over, "Fat Thor" everybody's favorite
electric Asgardian just got a new, less fat-shamey

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:06.480
moniker.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.940
In advance of the digital and Blu Ray release
of Avengers: Endgame, Marvel Studios released

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.360
an extensive list of the special features
awaiting home viewers and one of those features

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.100
is entitled "The Creation of Bro Thor," which
is a slightly more charitable nickname.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.539
It's just the latest development in the ongoing
saga of… well, we suppose we're calling

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:28.330
him "Bro Thor" now, although we were always
partial to Tony Stark's christening of the

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.880
Thunder God as "Lebowski."

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.400
"Nobody calls me 'Lebowski.'

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.400
You've got the wrong guy.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.480
I'm The Dude, man."

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.320
In case you somehow weren't aware of the uproar
over the character's portly new physique in

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.620
Endgame, allow us to recap the madness for
you.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.140
In the film's first act, Thor out of sheer
rage and frustration unceremoniously decapitated

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.940
Thanos after the Avengers and Captain Marvel
tracked the Mad Titan down to his farm planet.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.900
It turned out that Thanos had essentially
set the Infinity Stones to self-destruct after

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.969
using them to complete his mission of wiping
out half of all life in the universe.

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.359
Without the stones, the Avengers had no way
to undo what had been done.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:07.640
The film then jumped forward five years, a
period during which our heroes had adjusted

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.690
to post-Decimation life in a variety of ways.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:14.440
Natasha Romanoff desperately struggled to
keep all of Earth's defenders on the same

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.940
page in the hope of averting another catastrophe.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.260
Bruce Banner found a way to retain his smarts
and personality after Hulking out.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.140
"Eighteen months in the gamma lab.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.800
I put the brains and the brawn together.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.620
And now look at me.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.900
Best of both worlds."

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.440
Tony Stark got married and had a precocious
daughter who loved him 3000.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:35.450
As for Thor?

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.320
Uhh, well …

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.720
"I think I'm having a panic attack."

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:38.780
"Get it together!"

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:44.180
Well, Thor retired to the New Asgard settlement
in Norway to play Fortnite with Korg, drink

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:48.330
all of the beer he could possibly get his
hands on, and put on just a few pounds.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.990
Recruited by Banner and Rocket to take part
in the Avengers' audacious plan to travel

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.970
back to various periods in time to secure
the Infinity Stones before Thanos could, Odinson

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.480
came along only half-willingly.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.940
For a good portion of the film especially
during his encounter with his mother Frigga

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.250
during a jaunt back to Asgard in 2013 it was
obvious that his physical changes were a result

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.240
of a deep depression.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.620
At a crucial moment, he had failed his friends
and the planet he had sworn to protect by

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:18.250
way of not going for Thanos' head, an oversight
which gave the Mad Titan the opportunity to

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.820
snap his big purple fingers and make the Avengers'
worst fear a reality.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.780
"You should have gone for the head."

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:28.840
"NOOO—"

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.440
Now, we should mention that during Endgame,
a few tasteless jokes were lobbed Thor's way.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:39.100
These jokes provoked the ire of a sizable
swath of the internet, as many felt that the

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.730
character was being fat-shamed, and that his
depression was used as a device to make him

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.300
the butt of simplistic gags.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.820
Still others, though, read the situation a
bit differently.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.920
Sure, Stark had a few snarky things to say
about Thor's round waistline; we submit that

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.231
this is because he was Tony Stark, and it
would've been completely out of character

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.860
for him to not lob a few zingers at his friend.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.600
Further, Hemsworth gave an absolutely brilliant
performance which managed to hit comedic notes

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.820
while being a completely relatable illustration
of the realities of depression and don't even

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:11.440
get us started on the fact that, despite sinking
to his lowest point, he was still worthy of

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.940
wielding his beloved Mjolnir.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.740
"Are you crying?"

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.280
"No!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.380
…...Yes."

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.160
We're not crying you're crying!

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.300
Screenwriters Christopher Markus and Stephen
McFeely have even stated that it was their

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:28.910
intention to use Thor's fragile mental state
to humanize the Asgardian to a degree and

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.220
in our humble opinion, they pulled that off
smashingly.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.960
Well, to no one's surprise, it seems that
Marvel Studios must have caught wind of the

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:39.190
whole brouhaha, and made the understandable
decision that the "fat" descriptor just wasn't

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.990
going to work for official purposes.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.550
We think it's a laudable choice.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.580
How will the ever-polarized internet respond?

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.720
All we can do is wait and find out.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.040
Fortunately for Marvel Studios, they make
movies that are beloved by you, everybody

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.250
you know, everybody they know, and so on.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.380
But even the MCU can't please everybody, and
we sincerely doubt that Marvel even feels

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.000
pressured to try at this point.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.340
Renaming the stocky Asgardian "Bro Thor" was
a thoughtful move, and one that shows that

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.780
the House of Ideas isn't into shaming anybody.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.460
Except, of course, for bros.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:12.260
We can expect an overwhelming wave of indignation
from the online bro community at any moment.

